Maintainer: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), libsdl3-dev, libgl-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://www.classicube.net/

Package: classicube
Architecture: ppc64
# dlopen'd, so shlibs can't see them: OpenAL (sound) and libcrypto (system certificates for its HTTPS
# downloads); SDL3 is linked (shlibs)
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libopenal1, libssl3t64
Suggests: classicube-data
Description: ClassiCube block building game
 A Minecraft Classic compatible game (SDL3 window and gamepad, desktop GL 1, OpenAL), fullscreen
 by default (options.txt win-fullscreen=false for a window).
 /usr/games/classicube runs it from a per-user directory (~/.local/share/classicube), where it
 keeps options, maps and screenshots. It does not contain Mojang's textures, sounds and music:
 the game's launcher downloads them on first run, or classicube-data (licensed, a separate
 source package) installs them. See /usr/share/doc/classicube/README.Debian.
